{"assessment":{"adaptation_action":"merge-into-rule","applicability":"adapt","candidate_domains":["general"],"rationale":"IT-STE needs one vocabulary-admission rule for approved general words and recognized domain terms; the ASD dictionary and technical-term model require an IT-specific terminology framework.","status":"reviewed"},"schema_version":"1.0.0","source":{"block_id":"1.1","kind":"rule","physical_pdf_pages":[46,46],"revision":"r0001","standard":"asd-ste100","title":"Use words that are: - Approved in the dictionary - Technical nouns - Technical verbs.","version":"issue-9"},"target_rule_ids":["ITSTE-R-0001"]}
{"assessment":{"adaptation_action":"merge-into-rule","applicability":"adapt","candidate_domains":["general"],"rationale":"Part of speech is a core lexical-entry constraint and belongs with approved meaning, permitted forms, and noun-verb treatment in one IT-STE term-use rule.","status":"reviewed"},"schema_version":"1.0.0","source":{"block_id":"1.2","kind":"rule","physical_pdf_pages":[46,48],"revision":"r0001","standard":"asd-ste100","title":"Use approved words from the dictionary only as the specified part of speech.","version":"issue-9"},"target_rule_ids":["ITSTE-R-0002"]}
{"assessment":{"adaptation_action":"merge-into-rule","applicability":"adapt","candidate_domains":["general"],"rationale":"Approved meaning is necessary to control ordinary and overloaded IT senses and belongs with the part-of-speech and form constraints for the same lexical entry.","status":"reviewed"},"schema_version":"1.0.0","source":{"block_id":"1.3","kind":"rule","physical_pdf_pages":[48,48],"revision":"r0001","standard":"asd-ste100","title":"Use approved words only with their approved meanings.","version":"issue-9"},"target_rule_ids":["ITSTE-R-0002"]}
{"assessment":{"adaptation_action":"merge-into-rule","applicability":"adapt","candidate_domains":["general"],"rationale":"Permitted forms belong to the same lexical-entry contract as part of speech and meaning; IT-STE must record applicable forms without importing ASD-specific dictionary tables.","status":"reviewed"},"schema_version":"1.0.0","source":{"block_id":"1.4","kind":"rule","physical_pdf_pages":[48,49],"revision":"r0001","standard":"asd-ste100","title":"Use only the approved forms of verbs and adjectives.","version":"issue-9"},"target_rule_ids":["ITSTE-R-0002"]}
{"assessment":{"adaptation_action":"merge-into-rule","applicability":"adapt","candidate_domains":["general"],"rationale":"The domain-term principle applies, but the ASD category inventory does not map directly to IT; IT-STE must admit terms through authoritative IT and product terminology.","status":"reviewed"},"schema_version":"1.0.0","source":{"block_id":"1.5","kind":"rule","physical_pdf_pages":[49,53],"revision":"r0001","standard":"asd-ste100","title":"You can use words that you can include in a technical noun category.","version":"issue-9"},"target_rule_ids":["ITSTE-R-0001"]}
{"assessment":{"adaptation_action":"merge-into-rule","applicability":"adapt","candidate_domains":["general"],"rationale":"IT content needs terms outside a general controlled vocabulary, but admission must depend on a recognized domain concept and context rather than only on noun position or an ASD category.","status":"reviewed"},"schema_version":"1.0.0","source":{"block_id":"1.6","kind":"rule","physical_pdf_pages":[53,54],"revision":"r0001","standard":"asd-ste100","title":"Use a word that is not approved in the dictionary, only when it is a technical noun or part of a technical noun.","version":"issue-9"},"target_rule_ids":["ITSTE-R-0001"]}
{"assessment":{"adaptation_action":"merge-into-rule","applicability":"adapt","candidate_domains":["general","software-documentation","api","cli","user-interface","source-code"],"rationale":"IT commonly has established noun-verb pairs, so approval for one part of speech must not imply approval for another; each function and meaning requires independent approval.","status":"reviewed"},"schema_version":"1.0.0","source":{"block_id":"1.7","kind":"rule","physical_pdf_pages":[55,55],"revision":"r0001","standard":"asd-ste100","title":"Do not use words that are technical nouns as verbs.","version":"issue-9"},"target_rule_ids":["ITSTE-R-0002"]}
{"assessment":{"adaptation_action":"merge-into-rule","applicability":"adapt","candidate_domains":["general","software-documentation","api","cli","user-interface","configuration","source-code"],"rationale":"IT content needs an authoritative term for each concept, but authority can come from standards, schemas, interfaces, product terminology, or project glossaries rather than only company or industry lists.","status":"reviewed"},"schema_version":"1.0.0","source":{"block_id":"1.8","kind":"rule","physical_pdf_pages":[55,55],"revision":"r0001","standard":"asd-ste100","title":"Use technical nouns that are approved in your company, industry, or subject field.","version":"issue-9"},"target_rule_ids":["ITSTE-R-0003"]}
{"assessment":{"adaptation_action":"merge-into-rule","applicability":"adapt","candidate_domains":["general","software-documentation","user-interface","error-messages","support-troubleshooting"],"rationale":"Concise terms improve comprehension, but a three-word ceiling can damage established IT terms and exact interface names; require the shortest unambiguous internationally understood term instead.","status":"reviewed"},"schema_version":"1.0.0","source":{"block_id":"1.9","kind":"rule","physical_pdf_pages":[56,56],"revision":"r0001","standard":"asd-ste100","title":"When you must select a technical noun, use one which is short and easy to understand.","version":"issue-9"},"target_rule_ids":["ITSTE-R-0004"]}
{"assessment":{"adaptation_action":"merge-into-rule","applicability":"adapt","candidate_domains":["general","software-documentation","user-interface","error-messages","support-troubleshooting"],"rationale":"Regional expressions, slang, and narrow internal jargon impede international comprehension; established IT terminology remains valid when it is widely recognized or clearly defined.","status":"reviewed"},"schema_version":"1.0.0","source":{"block_id":"1.10","kind":"rule","physical_pdf_pages":[56,56],"revision":"r0001","standard":"asd-ste100","title":"Do not use regional, slang, or jargon words as technical nouns.","version":"issue-9"},"target_rule_ids":["ITSTE-R-0004"]}
